@startuml registration-states
title Registration (R2 to R7) and waitlist entry (R6)
' Hand-written from the registration service: src/service/*, src/domain/registrationRules.ts and waitlistRules.ts;
' statuses in backend/packages/contracts/src/registrationEvents.ts. A seat is a row (ADR-0005).
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

state "Registration" as reg {
  state "Registered" as REGISTERED
  state "Withdrawn" as WITHDRAWN
  state "Cancelled" as CANCELLED
  [*] --> REGISTERED : R2 claims a free seat (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED); R7 may add above capacity, with no seat
  REGISTERED --> WITHDRAWN : R4, before the withdrawal deadline, frees the seat
  REGISTERED --> CANCELLED : the event is cancelled (R3, F4)
  WITHDRAWN --> [*]
  CANCELLED --> [*]
}

state "Waitlist entry" as wait {
  state "Waitlisted" as WAITLISTED
  state "Registered" as PROMOTED
  state "Withdrawn" as LEFT
  state "Cancelled" as WCANCELLED
  [*] --> WAITLISTED : R6, when the event is full
  WAITLISTED --> PROMOTED : the attendee registers (R2) or is added (R7); the entry names that registration
  WAITLISTED --> LEFT : the attendee leaves the waitlist
  WAITLISTED --> WCANCELLED : the event is cancelled
  PROMOTED --> [*]
  LEFT --> [*]
  WCANCELLED --> [*]
}

note bottom of reg
  At most one Registered row per attendee and event, and per seat
  (partial unique indexes). Registering again after withdrawing is a new row.
  Nobody is promoted automatically: a withdrawal or a capacity increase that opens a
  place only notifies the waiting attendees (R6), who then register for themselves.
end note
@enduml
